# EMS UI rule: hide raw IDs

- Do not display internal database identifiers (for example `id`, `siteId`, `departmentId`) directly in UI views.
- When row reference is needed, show a serial number (`#`, index-based) or business-friendly field (code, name, employee number).
- Keep IDs for internal keys, routing, API payloads, and state management only.
- Avoid labels/messages like `Id 123` in user-visible text; prefer friendly fallbacks like `Unknown` or `Not assigned`.
- For any dropdown/select/search-picker UI (including task assignment), display business labels only (for example employee names/codes). Never show labels/messages like `Employee ID`.
- Option values may still carry internal IDs for wiring, but the UI must not present them to the user (including search placeholder text).
